      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2009 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A series of 3-amino-6-aryl-pyridazines have been identified as CB(2) agonists with high efficacy and selectivity against the CB(1) receptor. Details of the investigation of structure-activity relationships (SAR) are disclosed, which led to the identification of pyridazine analogue 35, a compound with high potency in an in vivo model of inflammatory pain."
      },
